---
// Controls bound to memory.ts's withKnowledge call (see learn/playground.ts, `data-control`, and
// lessons/connected-memory/config-edit.ts). Each writes one line of the call and runs the code again. A value the
// kernel does not take is written as given, and withKnowledge refuses it in its own words.
---

<div class="learn-controls">
  <label>
    <span>limit</span>
    <input type="number" min="1" max="50" step="1" data-control="limit" />
    <small>The most memories ranked first that a request is sent. The kernel takes 1 to 50.</small>
  </label>
  <label>
    <span>walk</span>
    <input type="number" min="0" max="10" step="1" data-control="walk" />
    <small>How many more places the walk by subject may add. The kernel takes 0 to 10.</small>
  </label>
</div>
<p class="learn-note" data-controls-note hidden>
  A control is greyed out when its line is missing from your code. Press Reset in the Code pane to bring it back.
</p>
